            <ArticleTitle>Ectopic lobe of right lung with abscess formation in children: a visual diagnosis case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>932-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0b013e31829ec507</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 9-year-old boy who had chest pain of 3 weeks' duration caused by ectopic lobe of the right lung with abscess formation. The diagnosis was supported by chest computed tomography and video-assisted thoracoscopy. The child responded well to the operation and fully recovered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
